## Endorsement date validator updated to match 90-day product configuration for homeowners policies.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-700005)
**Module:** PolicyCenter | **Category:** ConfigurationError | **Severity:** SEV2-High
**Resolution Type:** CodeFix
**Date:** 2025-12-03
**Guidewire Version:** Jasper

### Summary / Symptom
Endorsement effective date validation is rejecting valid future dates for homeowners policies. Agents entering an endorsement effective date more than 30 days in the future receive a validation error saying the date is out of range, even though the product rules allow up to 90 days. This started after last week's product configuration update.

### Resolution
The issue was caused by a hardcoded 30-day maximum in the endorsement effective date validator, which conflicted with the product configuration allowing up to 90 days. After a product configuration update, agents were incorrectly blocked from entering valid future dates. The validator was modified to dynamically read the allowed date range from the product configuration, resolving the mismatch and enabling agents to enter endorsement dates up to 90 days in the future.


